Z||000000||peterh||08-11-99||11:47 AM||||I just bought a 86 SE that needs some front end work. My mechanic say it needs lower ball joints, upper control arm buchins and a rack and pinion. According to the 2 manuals I have the lower ball joints are welded in? and you have to replace the entire control arm. Same with the upper control for new bushings. I have the Fiero store catalog which lists ball joints and bushings but no mention of control arms. Also where can I get a better price on the rack and pinion than the Fiero store, they want $200?<br>This is my first entry and I have enjoyed reading the funny and informative stuff posted here.<br>
Z||000001||theogre||08-11-99||01:11 PM||||always try your local parts dealers before calling F.S....... <p>For bushings also try  <A HREF="http://www.suspension.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.suspension.com/</A>  as well.<p>The lowers (ball joints) are pressed in. they may have a tavk weld that needs to be carfully ground off, but as far as I know they are pressed parts, and are replaceable sans the arm.
Z||000002||VISCERAL||08-11-99||01:54 PM||||Try Pep Boys for the rack. It's $100 but, it's got plastic bushings that'll only last about 65-75k miles. then you'll need another bushing by then. 
Z||000003||Cooter||08-11-99||08:21 PM||||$100 for a rack? Mine started making the bumping noise so I parked it in the driveway with a for sale on it. I guess that I will have to fix the damn thing if it only costs 100 bucks. Seeing as how my car has about 60,000 miles on it now and the original rack lasted this long- 14 years- maybe the PepBoys rack will be good for another 14 years. Do you think my Iron Duck will last that long????
